Purgatorios wrote:
>
> This a big deal for me! Definitely the farthest I've gotten by far.
>
> Should I use my (probable) wish from the blessed magic lamp or wait
> longer to see if I will need it?  If so, on what?

You have the two best weapons but mediocre armor.  You have seen the
Castle so abundant wishes are around the corner.  I favor keeping it for
the permanent light source.

> Should I use excalibur or grayswandir?

Excalibur to explore.  Switching to Grayswandir for combat.  Exercise
twoweapon towards maximum.  Don't bother switching weaspons for monsters
weaker than your current level facing only one at a time - Two weapon
gets exercised anyways.

You're also at a point where you should have a lot of arrows and maximum
luck so start moving bow towards expert.  Multifiring arrows sure takes
out a crwod before they can hit you with their melee weapons.

> Should I spend my scrolls of enchant weapon/armor, magic marker etc.
> or wait until I get better stuff?

The enchant weapon definitely.  Dip for water so you have lots of holy
water then read them blessed.  The more enchanted the better the
searching function for Excalibur.  The more enchanted the meaner the
monsters that Grayswandir can take out in one whack.

> What should I genocide?

Bless one and go with L.  Some folks like ;  but I use missiles against
them.  I like to do the two types of mind flayer individually after L
then R - A total of 4 scrolls 2 blessed 2 uncursed.

> Since I have polycontrol and polymorph should I try to eat rings or
> something crazy like that?

I don't use either when playing samurai.

> Magic trap dancing and then succubus wrasslin'?

Maybe and yes.

> chaotic altar on lvl 11

I like to keep one cross aligned altar just in case.  I convert the
rest.

> castle on 25 (ran away as soon as I saw it, farthest I've gotten)

Once L are gone you're good to go.  As it is you may be able to handle
it as long as the L are not purple.

> quest entrance on 12 (haven't done it, have never done a quest)

Go for it.

> some pet dogs running around, nothing awesome
>
> LVL 13 Samurai
> St: 18/19   Dx: 18  Co: 18  In: 11 Wi: 13 Ch: 9
> HP 145(145) PW 57(57) AC: -12 T: 31561

You don't list XP.  When enhancing skills more is better so there's a
trade off between more skill slots for multifire missile and stronger
monster generation.

> Intrinsics:
>
> cold resist
> poison resist
> telepathy
> see invis
> fire resist
> speed

No reflection or MR.  Among those only poison resistance has as much
priority.

> weapon skills:
> twoweapon: unskilled
> long sword: expert
> saber: basic
> bow: skilled
> spells: attack and clerical unskilled

Probably not worth enhancing spells until you have XP slots to spare. 
You will get a huge gain from bow to expert and a smaller but large gain
from moving twoweapon up.

> Wearing:
> uncursed amulet of unchanging

You got the bag of holding in Sokoban.  Bad luck but not fatal.  Time to
look for reflection here or with SDSM from the Castle wand wish.

> ring of slow digestion
> blessed rustproof +3 excalibur in main hand
> +2 katana in other hand
> uncursed +2 pair of yugake
> blessed +3 pair of jumping boots
> blessed +0 dwarvish iron helm

Nice armor would be nice but jumping boots are beneficial enough in the
final level that it might be worth enchanting to max now.

> uncursed burnt +2 robe

If you can get MR from other source this is an excellent cloak.  But MR
is very high priority so it might end up in reserve.

> blessed +1 blue dragon scale mail

Switch to SDSM or GDSM with a wand wish soon.

> 20275 gold

Find a priest and spend it on protection.

> Weapons:
> rustproof +0 snickersnee

In a chest so it can not be used against you.

> blessed +0 grayswandir
> yumi
> some ya and arrows

I would keep them in open inventory with the ya or arrows in the quiver.
Switch to bow, blast an oncoming crowd, switch to Grayswandir for close
combat, switch back to Excalibur to explore.  Dual wield either of the
melee weapons with your katana.

> halberd

Fun at either castle door if you are already skilled.  Otherwise heavy
enough that while in a chest with Snickersnee normal monsters can't pick
up the chest.  Rocks also work well to make the chest too heavy.

> Armor
> cursed amulet of stranglin'
> uncursed +0 elven shield
> uncursed +0 elven boots
> blessed +4 crystal plate mail
> elven leather helm, +1 yugake

More stuff to make the chest too heavy to pick up.

> Scrolls

Most should be blessed first.

> blessed scroll of enchant weapon

Excalibur to +5 or better.

> 2 blessed ID

So much for anything not being identified.

> 2 uncursed genocide

Bless then L+R.

> 2 blessed remove curse

So much for any item being cursed.

> blessed magic map

Permantent light.

> 2 uncursed enchant weapon
> uncursed enchant armor

Bless first.  Then Grayswandir and max out the boots.

> cursed genocide

Nurses.

> 2 cursed create monster

Do you want a sacrifest.

> uncursed taming

May be nice on Astral

> etc. etc. crappier scrolls

Dip some for blanks to write enchant weap/arm

> Spells:

Good source of confusion

> Potions

Great for alchemy and other.

> blessed water

Make clones.

> uncursed gain ability
> uncursed enlighten

Bless these first.

> cursed water

Especially once you have 2+ every once in a while it is great to be able
to curse an object for tactical reasons.

> uncursed confusion

You want more of thse to fix armor later.

> Rings
> lev

Good for specific purposes

> 2 conflict

One is good for specific levels.

> Tools
> magic marker (0:49)

Woo who!  Enchantment time.

> sack

For the dangerous items

> 2blessed bag of holding

Nice to have a spare.

> blessed unicorn horn

Crucial gear.

> uncursed luckstone

Bless soonest


